{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And all the days of Enoch were five and sixty years and three hundred years.</b> All the days of his life were 365 years, equal to the number of the days of the sun, neither less nor more, for this righteous man knew and grasped the course of the sun and its mighty forces, and recognized through his wisdom that there is a supernal cause over all, and he cleaved to it. And I have already informed you above that there are lights for the lights, and all of them are drawn from the supernal light which this righteous man merited; and this is why Scripture used of him the expression ויהי — something you will not find regarding the earlier generations, of none of whom did it say anything but ויהיו — in order to hint that he was exalted in the supernal light concerning which it is written יהי אור ויהי אור. And we find this same expression also regarding Moses, peace be upon him; as it is written ויהי משה בהר, and through this he merited the light of the Torah that was given through him and he merited the radiance of the skin of his face. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:30.214906275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}